/-!
The Grassmannian endomorphism reduction and the honest-pair filtration of the truncated core.

The endomorphism step is proved through a finite coefficient cover. Given any core map
`π : CoreBaseRing a b c →ₗ[ℂ] V`, the cover is the current-cyclic span of `π` in the space of
linear maps from the coefficient ring to `V`. Coefficient multiplication acts by precomposition
and commutes with the pointwise current action. Newton reconstruction proves that every
coefficient translate is in this cyclic span. Evaluation at the unit is onto `V` when `π 1`
is cyclic. The cover is finite, satisfies all four fields of `CoreRelations`, and inherits the
site-count truncation. Thus `truncatedCoreRankBound_iff_coefficientBound` reduces the original
rank problem to finite cyclic cores with a commuting coefficient action, with no additional hypothesis.
No coefficient action on an arbitrary quotient `V` is asserted. The cover supplies exactly the
endomorphism reduction needed for upper bounds without constructing an infinite presented module.

`CoreCellFlag` records the existing ordered two-Grassmannian ideals, their one-dimensional
spanning steps, and their characteristic-polynomial relations. `coreCellFlag_exists` supplies
such a flag for every nonnegative triple. `coreCellFiltration` takes current spans of the ideal
images. These terms are increasing, current-stable, start at zero, and exhaust every cyclic
core. `coreIdealSpan_eq_coefficientSpan` identifies them with ideal multiples of the whole
module when the commuting coefficient action is present. `coreCellPiece_cyclic` proves that
each successive quotient is generated by its cell vector. `coreCellFiltration_finrank_le`
sums arbitrary proved cell rank estimates. These statements are valid for all triples, and in
particular for adjoint count one with arbitrary middle and central counts.

Partial current truncation is also proved: the positive parabolic currents annihilate the cell
vectors; the zero Cartan modes have weight `(a,b,a)`; and the positive Cartan modes land in the
preceding term. Nilpotence of the Grassmannian power sums supplies the latter assertion without
assuming a grading on the chosen spanning flag.

**Not proved here:** `CoreCellTruncation a b c Q π F`. Its conclusion requires every
root current at or above the union size to send the cell generator into the preceding term.
The negative parabolic roots, the middle lowering root, and the middle raising root are not
discharged in this file. `coreCellTruncation_piece` only proves that this generator statement implies
annihilation of the whole cyclic cell piece. It explicitly retains the truncation hypothesis.
The subset-cell raising annihilator, the two per-cell rank estimates, and the final
single-adjoint count are not proved here.
No theorem of type `TruncatedCoreRankBound 1 b c` is asserted.

The flag interface records only the proved spanning and characteristic properties. Any
raising annihilator property tied to recursive choices must be proved for a compatible flag;
it is not an implicit property of the noncomputably selected `coreCellFlag`.

This audit checks all declarations of the seven core modules imported above together with the
converted core leaf.
-/

